<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Polarity</h1>
<p>Sphere: Divine Sphere
Class: Druid (guild level 120)
Mana: 30, and more (see below)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>cast polarity &lt;target&gt;
</pre>
<p>A spell to turn the tables if there ever was. The caster grabs hold of 
the target and meditates on changing them, and the target's alignment is 
reversed: the good become just as evil, the evil just as good, and the 
neutral stay about where they are (see <a cmd='#'>Help Alignment</a>). The target only 
feels a bit disoriented.
</p><p>Turning someone costs extra mana besides the spell's own: half the 
target's level for a monster, and twice their level for a player. If you 
don't have it, the spell fails. You can't cast it on yourself, and on 
another player only if you have both signed the Book of Blood. Casting it 
is an attack. You must be standing. It is also found on scrolls, wands 
and staffs.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Alignment</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Divine Sphere</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Druid Spells</a>
</pre>




</div>